    "result_text": "The build is green \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` and `BUILD SUCCESS`, including the `coreMembershipNumberFormat` acceptance test.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `membershipNumber` as a derived, read-only field formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nBecause the value is a pure function of the owner's own persisted fields, I followed the repo's closest existing convention \u2014 `displayName`/`initials`, which are derived in the MapStruct mapper rather than stored in a column or assigned via a pipeline step:\n\n- **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `membershipNumber` property (read-only) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and it's serialized on both create and GET responses.\n- **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that composes `customerCode + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", registrationDate.getYear() % 100)`, guarding for null `customerCode`/`registrationDate` so seed owners (which have neither) map to a null membership number instead of throwing.\n\nNo entity, DB schema, or OfficeFloor pipeline changes were needed since nothing is persisted; the value derives at response time from fields the create pipeline already sets (`customerCode` via `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`, `registrationDate` via `BuildOwner`).",
